# PrivateBin previewed a pasted SVG attachment inline from a blob built with
# the attachment's own declared mime type, so scripts embedded in the SVG ran
# in the instance's origin when the preview rendered or the blob URL was
# opened directly (stored cross-site scripting through unsanitized active
# content, CWE-79; CVE-2022-24833). AttachmentViewer.setAttachment in
# js/privatebin.js base64-decodes the attachment, mints a same-origin object
# URL from it, puts that URL on the download link's href and hands it to the
# preview element; svg is one of the three content types a browser parses as
# markup and scripts in the creating origin. The fixing commit 2a4d572c1e
# ("Sanitize SVG preview, preventing script execution in instance context,
# while dropping support for attachment download in IE") routes image/svg
# mime types through DOMPurify.sanitize(decodedData, {USE_PROFILES: {svg:
# true, svgFilters: true}}) before the preview's blob is built, and factors
# the blob construction into a getBlobUrl helper. No pool correction.
#
# Held ATTENTION at recheck, content-conditional sanitisation: the preview
# pipeline exists, svg alone among the previewed image types carries script
# semantics, and the gap is the missing per-type sanitise branch -- the same
# type-branch-completeness family as the unquoted bind type and the
# first-quote-only replace.
#
# Measured at recheck against the current knowledge base, not inherited. The
# first pass recorded "zero findings at both revisions" and read the cause as
# no labelled path connecting a DOMPurify-credited control to an img
# element. Re-tracing found a different and larger cause: the whole
# application body of js/privatebin.js was not being extracted at all. The
# file is one assignment whose value is an immediately-invoked function
# expression -- jQuery.PrivateBin = (function($, RawDeflate) { ... }(jQuery));
# -- and lowering evaluated a call's callee only when it was an attribute
# (receiver) or another call, so the invoked function's body never lowered.
# The file reported 24 code.Call nodes with the highest at line 45 of 5495,
# and 5 analysis.function.context nodes; everything from the module wrapper
# to the end of the file was invisible to every binding. Three --cache off
# scans per revision (timeout 180, --max-ram 6GB) reported 147/147/147
# findings at 2a4d572c1e^ and 147/147/147 at 2a4d572c1e, none in
# js/privatebin.js.
#
# The last two tests are the minimal pair for that construct: identical
# bodies, differing only in whether the wrapper is an expression statement --
# which the frontend already splices into the module -- or the value of an
# assignment. A call whose callee is a function expression now lowers that
# body, unwrapping the parenthesized-expression chain so both
# `(function () { ... })()` and `(function () { ... }())` spell the same
# thing, and both members of the pair report. With the file visible, three
# --cache off scans per revision report 165/165/165 findings at both
# revisions, 58 rows inside js/privatebin.js at each, 1815 code.Call nodes
# and 280 function contexts in the file; the per-rule multisets are identical
# between the revisions, so no shipped rule discriminates the fix.
#
# The discriminating binding for the weakness itself was measured and is not
# shipped. A presence binding on the sibling shape of the served-response
# form -- a function that mints an object URL from a blob whose type comes
# from a runtime value, with no active-content type or sanitizer named --
# reports 2 function contexts on the vulnerable revision and 2 on the fixed
# one before neutralisers, and 1 and 1 after them: the fix factors the blob
# construction into getBlobUrl, which contains the blob and the object URL
# but no sanitizer, so the function-scoped binding fires on that helper at
# both revisions while the sanitizer sits in its caller -- the same
# fix-in-the-callee, label-in-the-caller shape measured non-discriminating
# before. Keying instead on the function that both builds and consumes the
# URL would encode this fix's own layout, and the shape is ordinary code
# anyway: across nine collateral checkouts the probe reports 14 function
# contexts (autogpt frontend 10, chatwoot 2, BookStack 1, brave-core 1,
# appsmith, drawio, audiobookshelf and coolify 0), 11 of them still standing
# after the neutraliser list, and the survivors are download helpers that
# build a blob from generated bytes and hand its URL to an anchor. When
# content-conditional-sanitise vocabulary lands, the raw blob preview below
# must flip to expect.

test "rank1607: svg attachments preview from a raw blob"
  lang javascript
  file js/privatebin.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  me.setAttachment = function (attachmentData, fileName) {
      const mimeTypeEnd = attachmentData.indexOf(';');
      const mimeType = attachmentData.substring(5, mimeTypeEnd);
      const rawData = attachmentData.substring(attachmentData.indexOf(',') + 1);
      const decodedData = rawData.length > 0 ? atob(rawData) : '';

      const blob = new window.Blob([decodedData], { type: mimeType });
      const blobUrl = window.URL.createObjectURL(blob);
      $attachmentLink.attr('href', blobUrl);

      me.handleBlobAttachmentPreview($attachmentPreview, blobUrl, mimeType);
  };
  ```

test "rank1607: the fixed revision sanitizes svg before the blob"
  lang javascript
  file js/privatebin.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  const purifySvgConfig = {
      USE_PROFILES: {
          svg: true,
          svgFilters: true
      }
  };

  me.setAttachment = function (attachmentData, fileName) {
      const mimeTypeEnd = attachmentData.indexOf(';');
      const mimeType = attachmentData.substring(5, mimeTypeEnd);
      const rawData = attachmentData.substring(attachmentData.indexOf(',') + 1);
      const decodedData = rawData.length > 0 ? atob(rawData) : '';

      let blobUrl = getBlobUrl(decodedData, mimeType);
      $attachmentLink.attr('href', blobUrl);

      if (mimeType.match(/image\/svg/i)) {
          const sanitizedData = DOMPurify.sanitize(decodedData, purifySvgConfig);
          blobUrl = getBlobUrl(sanitizedData, mimeType);
      }

      me.handleBlobAttachmentPreview($attachmentPreview, blobUrl, mimeType);
  };
  ```

test "rank1607: the preview element loads the object url it was handed"
  lang javascript
  file js/privatebin.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-004
  code
  ```
  me.handleBlobAttachmentPreview = function ($targetElement, blobUrl, mimeType) {
      if (blobUrl) {
          if (mimeType.match(/image\//i)) {
              $targetElement.html(
                  $(document.createElement('img'))
                      .attr('src', blobUrl)
                      .attr('class', 'img-thumbnail')
              );
          }
      }
  };
  ```

